Z||000000||Ben84||05-14-2001||06:40 PM||||Today, while driving from work....my 85 2m6 started to make a strange noise from the engine compartment.... It makes a (cha, cha, cha, cha) noise.... There is no noticeable change in the performance...just the noise from the engine compartment.  I'm praying for small repair bill, if I'm not able to repair my self... I need to know some of the possible causes.... Belts, fluid level, and charging systems are fine.  Thanks||||reg||8
Z||000001||FieroJoe||05-14-2001||09:17 PM||||Hehe, well if your hearing "cha-cha-cha" from your engine, you better pull over and make sure you dont have a party going on inside there!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Anyways, describe the noise a little better please.  Does it sound like something is spinning and making this sound (bearing?), or just a rattle?  Hopefully it is just a rattle or something.  Check to see if one of your engine vents is shaking against the post it sits on the decklid, or maybe your air cleaner canister lid, or some bracket, or <I>something</I>.  Just throwing out ideas here.  Drive it again and see if it happens again, and note what else is going on when it does.  Like, certain RPM, engine warm or cold, certain speed, braking, turning, whatever!<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||05-14-2001||10:55 PM||||At the same time "Ka-thap-a-wok" vs "Ching-go-dang-dang" doesn't help either. If it makes the noise at idle, try to nail down the approximate location. A very long screwdriver to the ear (handle) can help.<P>High RPM? Low? Load? No load? Slow? Fast? Cruising? Floored? Turning? Straight? Stoned? Sober? etc....<P>TK||||reg||1
